{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":5508,"output":539,"cacheRead":35072,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":263,"totalTokens":41119,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"All 21 tests pass. The implementation is complete. Let me summarize what was done:\n\n1. Added `--max-pending-hours H` argument to the `check-anchors` subcommand\n2. Added `import time` to the imports\n3. Modified `cmd_check_anchors` to:\n   - Track Sigstore attestation times for range heads in `attestation_time` dict\n   - When processing an OTS proof for a range head that's pending, check if the attestation time is more than H hours ago\n   - Handle both orderings: OTS file processed before sigstore (checked in the ranges loop) and sigstore processed before OTS (checked during OTS processing)\n   - Print error message \"still pending N h\" to stderr when the condition is met\n   - Exit 1 if any range head's pending proof exceeds the threshold\n\nThe implementation satisfies all requirements:\n- Without the option, behavior is unchanged (pending proofs accepted, exit 0)\n- With the option, if any range head's proof is pending and its Sigstore attestation is more than H hours ago, exit 1 with message \"still pending N h\"\n- A pending proof younger than H hours is fine (exit 0)\n- All existing tests pass"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":5508,"output":539,"cacheRead":35072,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":263,"totalTokens":41119,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"All 21 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI've added the `--max-pending-hours H` option to `python3 record/record.py check-anchors` with the following behavior:\n\n1. **Without the option**: Behavior unchanged - pending OpenTimestamps proofs are accepted (exit 0).\n\n2. **With the option**: If any range head's OTS proof is still pending and its Sigstore attestation time is more than H hours ago:\n   - Exit code 1\n   - Prints to stderr: `BAD: anchors/NNNNNN.ots: still pending N h` (where N is the whole number of hours since attestation)\n\n3. **Pending proof younger than H hours**: Accepted (exit 0).\n\n4. **Confirmed (non-pending) proofs**: Always accepted regardless of age.\n\n5. **Missing OTS proofs**: Still caught as before (existing behavior preserved).\n\nThe implementation handles both file processing orders (`.ots` before `.sigstore.json` and vice versa) by checking:\n- During OTS file processing (if sigstore attestation time already known)\n- During the ranges loop after all anchors are processed (for the case where OTS file was processed first)\n\nAll 21 existing tests in `record/test_record.py` continue to pass."}}
