\"x\")\nResourceWarning: Enable tracemalloc to get the object allocation traceback\nok\ntest_verdict_must_come_from_someone_else (test_record.Ledger.test_verdict_must_come_from_someone_else) ... /workspace/record/test_record.py:30: ResourceWarning: unclosed file <_io.BufferedReader name='/tmp/tmp9cfvt18z/entries/000001.json'>\n  return {\"seq\": n, \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(open(self.entry(n), \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()}\nResourceWarning: Enable tracemalloc to get the object allocation traceback\nok\ntest_verdict_must_name_the_plan_by_hash (test_record.Ledger.test_verdict_must_name_the_plan_by_hash) ... /workspace/record/test_record.py:30: ResourceWarning: unclosed file <_io.BufferedReader name='/tmp/tmpto4zgh2s/entries/000001.json'>\n  return {\"seq\": n, \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(open(self.entry(n), \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()}\nResourceWarning: Enable tracemalloc to get the object allocation traceback\nok\ntest_wrong_data_exits_1_not_3 (test_record.Ledger.test_wrong_data_exits_1_not_3) ... /workspace/record/test_record.py:173: ResourceWarning: unclosed file <_io.BufferedReader name='/tmp/tmp066d18dh/entries/000001.json'>\n  raw = open(self.entry(1), \"rb\").read().replace(b'\"claim\":\"mlp beats linear\"', b'\"claim\":\"\\\\ud800\"')\nResourceWarning: Enable tracemalloc to get the object allocation traceback\n/workspace/record/test_record.py:174: ResourceWarning: unclosed file <_io.BufferedWriter name='/tmp/tmp066d18dh/entries/000001.json'>\n  open(self.entry(1), \"wb\").write(raw)\nResourceWarning: Enable tracemalloc to get the object allocation traceback\nok\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 21 tests in 0.073s\n\nOK (skipped=1)\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":154,"timestamp":1794739914443},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All tests pass. Now I need to implement the `--max-pending-hours` option. Let me analyze the `cmd_check_anchors` function more carefully.\n\nThe function:\n1. Loads the chain\n2. Iterates through anchors, checking both `.ots` and `.sigstore.json` files\n3. For `.ots` files, it calls `check_ots` which returns the earliest Bitcoin block time or `None` if pending\n4. For `.sigstore.json` files, it calls `check_sigstore` which returns the integrated time `t` (Sigstore attestation time)\n5. It tracks ranges from sigstore attestations and verifies every range head has an `.ots` proof\n6. It prints results and returns exit code\n\nI need to:\n1. Add `--max-pending-hours` argument to the check-anchors subparser\n2. In `cmd_check_anchors`, track the Sigstore attestation time for each range head\n3. When checking `.ots` proofs for range heads, if the proof is pending (returns `None`) and the attestation time is more than H hours ago, add a \"BAD\" error with the message \"still pending N h\"\n4. The whole number of hours N should be calculated as the floor of hours since attestation\n\nLet me implement this. I'll need to:\n- Store the attestation time for each range head (the `t` returned from `check_sigstore`)\n- When processing `.ots` files for range heads, check if pending and if so, compare with max_pending_hours\n- The current time should be `time.time()` or similar\n\nLet me look at the code structure again and make the edits.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"All tests pass. Now I need to implement the `--max-pending-hours` option. Let me analyze the `cmd_check_anchors` function more carefully.\\n\\nThe function:\\n1. Loads the chain\\n2. Iterates through anchors, checking both `.ots` and `.sigstore.json` files\\n3. For `.ots` files, it calls `check_ots` which returns the earliest Bitcoin block time or `None` if pending\\n4. For `.sigstore.json` files, it calls `check_sigstore` which returns the integrated time `t` (Sigstore attestation time)\\n5. It tracks ranges from sigstore attestations and verifies every range head has an `.ots` proof\\n6. It prints results and returns exit code\\n\\nI need to:\\n1. Add `--max-pending-hours` argument to the check-anchors subparser\\n2. In `cmd_check_anchors`, track the Sigstore attestation time for each range head\\n3. When checking `.ots` proofs for range heads, if the proof is pending (returns `None`) and the attestation time is more than H hours ago, add a \\\"BAD\\\" error with the message \\\"still pending N h\\\"\\n4. The whole number of hours N should be calculated as the floor of hours since attestation\\n\\nLet me implement this. I'll need to:\\n- Store the attestation time for each range head (the `t` returned from `check_sigstore`)\\n- When processing `.ots` files for range heads, check if pending and if so, compare with max_pending_hours\\n- The current time should be `time.time()` or similar\\n\\nLet me look at the code structure again and make the edits.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Now I'll implement the `--max-pending-hours` option. Let me make the necessary changes to `record.py`:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-dcc14872-432d-4ba3-9101-c89d216cf415","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/record/record.py","edits":[{"oldText":"    for name in (\"check-anchors\", \"monitor\"):\n        p = sub.add_parser(name)\n        p.add_argument(\"--repo\", default=\"5kasgard/exagium\")\n        p.add_argument(\"--workflow\", default=\".github/workflows/record.yml\")\n        if name == \"check-anchors\":\n            p.add_argument(\"--ref\", default=\"refs/heads/main\")\n            p.add_argument(\"--explorer\", action=\"append\", default=None,\n                           help=\"esplora API base; default blockstream.info and mempool.space\")\n        else:","newText":"    for name in (\"check-anchors\", \"monitor\"):\n        p = sub.add_parser(name)\n        p.add_argument(\"--repo\", default=\"5kasgard/exagium\")\n        p.add_argument(\"--workflow\", default=\".github/workflows/record.yml\")\n        if name == \"check-anchors\":\n            p.add_argument(\"--ref\", default=\"refs/heads/main\")\n            p.add_argument(\"--explorer\", action=\"append\", default=None,\n                           help=\"esplora API base; default blockstream.info and mempool.space\")\n            p.add_argument(\"--max-pending-hours\", type=int, metavar=\"H\",\n                           help=\"if a range head's OTS proof is still pending after H hours since its Sigstore attestation, exit 1\")\n        else:"},{"oldText":"def cmd_check_anchors(a):\n    \"\"\"Every anchor must be right, the writer's Sigstore ranges must cover entries 1..head with no gap or overlap,\n    and every range head must have its OpenTimestamps proof.\n    Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n    chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n    rows, bad, cant, ranges, stamped = [], [], [], [], set()\n    for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n        n = os.path.basename(path)\n        m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n        seq = int(m.group(1))\n        if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n            stamped.add(seq)\n        try:\n            if not 1 <= seq <= len(chain):\n                raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\")\n            raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n            if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n                t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n            else:\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n                    raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n                ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n                             \"writer_commit\": commit})\n        except Bad as ex:\n            bad.append(str(ex))\n        except CantCheck as ex:\n            cant.append(f\"anchors/{n}: {ex}\")\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        # the writer stamps every range head before it attests, and a failed stamp stops the run: a missing proof\n        # was removed (found by Z, 2026-11-06)\n        if hi not in stamped:\n            bad.append(f\"anchors/{hi:06d}.ots is missing, though the writer stamps every range head before attesting\")","newText":"def cmd_check_anchors(a):\n    \"\"\"Every anchor must be right, the writer's Sigstore ranges must cover entries 1..head with no gap or overlap,\n    and every range head must have its OpenTimestamps proof.\n    Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n    chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n    rows, bad, cant, ranges, stamped = [], [], [], [], set()\n    attestation_time = {}  # seq -> sigstore integrated time (for range heads)\n    for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n        n = os.path.basename(path)\n        m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n        seq = int(m.group(1))\n        if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n            stamped.add(seq)\n        try:\n            if not 1 <= seq <= len(chain):\n                raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\")\n            raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n            if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n                t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n                # If this is a range head with a pending proof, check max-pending-hours\n                if a.max_pending_hours is not None and seq in attestation_time and t is None:\n                    hours_pending = int((time.time() - attestation_time[seq]) // 3600)\n                    if hours_pending > a.max_pending_hours:\n                        bad.append(f\"anchors/{n}: still pending {hours_pending} h\")\n            else:\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n                    raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n                ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n                attestation_time[seq] = t\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n                             \"writer_commit\": commit})\n        except Bad as ex:\n            bad.append(str(ex))\n        except CantCheck as ex:\n            cant.append(f\"anchors/{n}: {ex}\")\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        # the writer stamps every range head before it attests, and a failed stamp stops the run: a missing proof\n        # was removed (found by Z, 2026-11-06)\n        if hi not in stamped:\n            bad.append(f\"anchors/{hi:06d}.ots is missing, though the writer stamps every range head before attesting\")\n        elif a.max_pending_hours is not None and hi in attestation_time:\n            # The .ots file exists but we haven't checked its pending status yet (ots files are processed before sigstore)\n            # Re-check by reading the proof result from rows\n            for row in rows:\n                if row[\"anchor\"] == f\"{hi:06d}.ots\" and row[\"existed_by\"] == \"pending\":\n                    hours_pending = int((time.time() - attestation_time[hi]) // 3600)\n                    if hours_pending > a.max_pending_hours:\n                        bad.append(f\"anchors/{hi:06d}.ots: still pending {hours_pending} h\")\n                    break"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":2550,"output":2430,"cacheRead":17536,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":359,"totalTokens":22516,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794739914445,"responseId":"gen-1794739914-jhCVr0VWrrArCQYE0Lfi","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":58460,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-dcc14872-432d-4ba3-9101-c89d216cf415","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 2 block(s) in /workspace/record/record.py."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 385     and every range head must have its OpenTimestamps proof.\n 386     Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n 387     chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n 388     rows, bad, cant, ranges, stamped = [], [], [], [], set()\n+389     attestation_time = {}  # seq -> sigstore integrated time (for range heads)\n 389     for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n 390         n = os.path.basename(path)\n 391         m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n 392         seq = int(m.group(1))\n     ...\n 398             raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n 399             if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n 400                 t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n 401                 rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n+403 