e `R.main` returns an int but I'm trying to unpack it as a tuple.\n\nActually, looking at my test code:\n```python\nrc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors'])\n```\n\nBut `R.main` only returns the exit code (an int), not a tuple. The existing test code uses `run_cmd` which captures stdout/stderr. Let me fix my test.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The issue is that the `check_sigstore` stub returns a tuple but the code expects it to return a tuple of 3 values. Let me fix the stub - it seems the issue is that the code is trying to unpack the return value but getting an int. Wait, the error says \\\"cannot unpack non-iterable int object\\\" - that's strange. Let me look at the code again.\\n\\nActually, looking at the error, it seems like the function returned just an int instead of a tuple. But my stub returns a tuple. Let me check if there's something else going on.\\n\\nWait, the error happens at line 50 which is the first `R.main` call. The output shows the JSON was printed, so the command ran but then there was an error. The error might be in the test script itself, not in the record.py code.\\n\\nLet me re-read the error: \\\"TypeError: cannot unpack non-iterable int object\\\" - this is in the test script at line 50. But the JSON output was printed successfully with rc=0 (since \\\"wrong\\\" is empty). The issue is probably that the `R.main` returns an int but I'm trying to unpack it as a tuple.\\n\\nActually, looking at my test code:\\n```python\\nrc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors'])\\n```\\n\\nBut `R.main` only returns the exit code (an int), not a tuple. The existing test code uses `run_cmd` which captures stdout/stderr. Let me fix my test.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The test script has an issue - `R.main` returns only the exit code. Let me fix the test:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-dbdadcbd-791b-4ffc-a9d9-41ec5cde14d9","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport tempfile, os, json, hashlib, time, io, contextlib, sys\nimport record as R\n\n# Create a test ledger\nd = tempfile.mkdtemp()\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'entries'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'anchors'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'inbox'))\n\n# Create two entries\nchain = []\nfor i in range(2):\n    kind = 'plan'\n    body = {'by': 'test', 'claim': f'claim {i+1}', 'test': 'test', 'decision_rule': 'rule'}\n    e = R.make_entry(chain, kind, body, now='2024-01-01T00:00:00Z')\n    raw = R.canonical(e)\n    with open(os.path.join(d, 'entries', f'{e[\\\"seq\\\"]:06d}.json'), 'wb') as f:\n        f.write(raw)\n    chain.append((e, hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()))\n\n# Create a sigstore anchor for entry 2 (range head)\n# We'll stub check_sigstore to return an old attestation time (73 hours ago)\nold_time = int(time.time()) - 73 * 3600  # 73 hours ago\n\n# Create dummy sigstore file\nwith open(os.path.join(d, 'anchors', '000002.sigstore.json'), 'w') as f:\n    f.write('{}')\n\n# Create dummy ots file\nwith open(os.path.join(d, 'anchors', '000002.ots'), 'wb') as f:\n    f.write(b'stub')\n\n# Stub the functions\noriginal_check_sigstore = R.check_sigstore\noriginal_check_ots = R.check_ots\n\ndef stub_check_sigstore(*args, **kwargs):\n    pred = R.range_predicate(chain, 1, 2)\n    return (old_time, pred, 'abc123')\n\ndef stub_check_ots(*args, **kwargs):\n    return None  # pending\n\nR.check_sigstore = stub_check_sigstore\nR.check_ots = stub_check_ots\n\ndef run_cmd(*args):\n    out, err = io.StringIO(), io.StringIO()\n    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(out), contextlib.redirect_stderr(err):\n        rc = R.main(['--ledger', d, *args])\n    return rc, out.getvalue(), err.getvalue()\n\ntry:\n    # Test without --max-pending-hours (should pass)\n    rc, out, err = run_cmd('check-anchors')\n    print(f'Without --max-pending-hours: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours 72 (should fail, 73 > 72)\n    rc, out, err = run_cmd('check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '72')\n    print(f'With --max-pending-hours 72: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours 73 (should pass, 73 > 73 is False)\n    rc, out, err = run_cmd('check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '73')\n    print(f'With --max-pending-hours 73: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours 74 (should pass, 73 < 74)\n    rc, out, err = run_cmd('check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '74')\n    print(f'With --max-pending-hours 74: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\nfinally:\n    R.check_sigstore = original_check_sigstore\n    R.check_ots = original_check_ots\n    import shutil\n    shutil.rmtree(d)\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":1107,"output":1285,"cacheRead":26304,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":326,"totalTokens":28696,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794740006934,"responseId":"gen-1794740006-YOXMj4lZ8q97Rdq0BGWE","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":19809,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-dbdadcbd-791b-4ffc-a9d9-41ec5cde14d9","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Without --max-pending-hours: rc=0\n  stderr: \nWith --max-pending-hours 72: rc=1\n  stderr: BAD: anchors/000002.ots: still pending 73 h\nWith --max-pending-hours 73: rc=0\n  stderr: \nWith --max-pending-hours 74: rc=0\n  stderr: \n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":62,"timestamp":1794740026805},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The feature works as expected:\n- Without `--max-pending-hours`: exit 0 (pending is accepted)\n- With `--max-pending-hours 72`: exit 1 with message \"still pending 73 h\" (73 > 72)\n- With `--max-pending-hours 73`: exit 0 (73 is not > 73)\n- With `--max-pending-hours 74`: exit 0 (73 < 74)\n\nThe message format matches the requirement: \"still pending N h\" where N is the whole number of hours.\n\nNow let me also test the case where the OTS proof is processed before the sigstore anchor (which is the case since .ots sorts before .sigstore.json). The code has a second check in the ranges loop for this case. Let me verify that works too.\n\nActually, wait - in my test, the .ots file is processed first (since it sorts before .sigstore.json), and at that point `attestation_time[seq]` is not yet populated. So the first check (in the ots processing block) won't trigger. But then the second check (in the ranges loop) should catch it because it looks at the rows for the pending status.\n\nLet me trace through the code:\n1. Process 000002.ots: `stamped.add(2)`, `check_ots` returns None, row added with \"existed_by\": \"pending\". `attestation_time[2]` doesn't exist yet, so the first check doesn't trigger.\n2. Process 000002.sigstore.json: `check_sigstore` returns old_time, `attestation_time[2] = old_time`, `ranges.append((1, 2, 'abc123'))`.\n3. Loop over ranges: `hi=2`, `hi in stamped` is True, so the missing proof check doesn't trigger. But then the `elif` block checks rows for \"000002.ots\" with \"existed_by\" == \"pending\" and finds it, computes hours_pending=73, and adds to bad if > max_pending_hours.\n\nThis is working correctly. Let me also test the case where the sigstore is processed first (if somehow the ordering was different). Actually, the sorting is deterministic by filename, so .ots always comes before .sigstore.json. But the code handles both cases.\n\nLet me also verify that a confirmed (non-pending) OTS proof doesn't trigger the check.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The feature works as expected:\\n- Without `--max-pending-hours`: exit 0 (pending is accepted)\\n- With `--max-pending-hours 72`: exit 1 with message \\\"still pending 73 h\\\" (73 > 72)\\n- With `--max-pending-hours 73`: exit 0 (73 is not > 73)\\n- With `--max-pending-hours 74`: exit 0 (73 < 74)\\n\\nThe message format matches the requirement: \\\"still pending N h\\\" where N is the whole number of hours.\\n\\nNow let me also test the case where the OTS proof is processed before the sigstore anchor (which is the case since .ots sorts before .sigstore.json). The code has a second check in the ranges loop for this case. Let me verify that works too.\\n\\nActually, wait - in my test, the .ots file is processed first (since it sorts before .sigstore.json), and at that point `attestation_time[seq]` is not yet populated. So the first check (in the ots processing block) won't trigger. But then the second check (in the ranges loop) should catch it because it looks at the rows for the pending status.\\n\\nLet me trace through the code:\\n1. Process 000002.ots: `stamped.add(2)`, `check_ots` returns None, row added with \\\"existed_by\\\": \\\"pending\\\". `attestation_time[2]` doesn't exist yet, so the first check doesn't trigger.\\n2. Process 000002.sigstore.json: `check_sigstore` returns old_time, `attestation_time[2] = old_time`, `ranges.append((1, 2, 'abc123'))`.\\n3. Loop over ranges: `hi=2`, `hi in stamped` is True, so the missing proof check doesn't trigger. But then the `elif` block checks rows for \\\"000002.ots\\\" with \\\"existed_by\\\" == \\\"pending\\\" and finds it, computes hours_pending=73, and adds to bad if > max_pending_hours.\\n\\nThis is working correctly. Let me also test the case where the sigstore is processed first (if somehow the ordering was different). Actually, the sorting is deterministic by filename, so .ots always comes before .sigstore.json. But the code handles both cases.\\n\\nLet me also verify that a confirmed (non-pending) OTS proof doesn't trigger the check.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The feature works correctly. Let me also test that a confirmed (non-pending) OTS proof doesn't trigger the check:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-49c31f7f-4211-4907-9626-165dc0ff6c22","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport tempfile, os, json, hashlib, time, io, contextlib, sys\nimport record as R\n\n# Create a test ledger\nd = tempfile.mkdtemp()\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'entries'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'anchors'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'inbox'))\n\n# Create two entries\nchain = []\nfor i in range(2):\n    kind = 'plan'\n    body = {'by': 'test', 'claim': f'claim {i+1}', 'test': 'test', 'decision_rule': 'rule'}\n    e = R.make_entry(chain, kind, body, now='2024-01-01T00:00:00Z')\n    raw = R.canonical(e)\n    with open(os.path.join(d, 'entries', f'{e[\\\"seq\\\"]:06d}.json'), 'wb') as f:\n        f.write(raw)\n    chain.append((e, hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()))\n\n# Create a sigstore anchor for entry 2 (range head)\nold_time = int(time.time()) - 73 * 3600  # 73 hours ago\n\n# Create dummy sigstore file\nwith open(os.path.join(d, 'anchors', '000002.sigstore.json'), 'w') as f:\n    f.write('{}')\n\n# Create dummy ots file\nwith open(os.path.join(d, 'anchors', '000002.ots'), 'wb') as f:\n    f.write(b'stub')\n\n# Stub the functions\noriginal_check_sigstore = R.check_sigstore\noriginal_check_ots = R.check_ots\n\ndef stub_check_sigstore(*args, **kwargs):\n    pred = R.range_predicate(chain, 1, 2)\n    return (old_time, pred, 'abc123')\n\n# Return a confirmed time (not pending)\nconfirmed_time = int(time.time()) - 10 * 3600  # 10 hours ago\ndef stub_check_ots_confirmed(*args, **kwargs):\n    return confirmed_time  # confirmed\n\nR.check_sigstore = stub_check_sigstore\nR.check_ots = stub_check_ots_confirmed\n\ndef run_cmd(*args):\n    out, err = io.StringIO(), io.StringIO()\n    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(out), contextlib.redirect_stderr(err):\n        rc = R.main(['--ledger', d, *args])\n    return rc, out.getvalue(), err.getvalue()\n\ntry:\n    # Test with --max-pending-hours 72 but confirmed proof (should pass)\n    rc, out, err = run_cmd('check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '72')\n    print(f'Confirmed proof with --max-pending-hours 72: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    print(f'  stdout: {out.strip()[:200]}')\nfinally:\n    R.check_sigstore = original_check_sigstore\n    R.check_ots = original_check_ots\n    import shutil\n    shutil.rmtree(d)\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":2504,"output":1305,"cacheRead":26304,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":538,"totalTokens":30113,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794740026807,"responseId":"gen-1794740026-2oF6mkUeqa0xEAErlsnD","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":25732,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-49c31f7f-4211-4907-9626-165dc0ff6c22","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed proof with --max-pending-hours 72: rc=0\n  stderr: \n  stdout: {\n \"anchors\": [\n  {\n   \"anchor\": \"000002.ots\",\n   \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\",\n   \"existed_by\": \"2026-11-15T00:54:12Z\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"anchor\": \"000002.sigstore.json\",\n   \"kind\": \"sigstore\",\n   \"entries\": \"\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":58,"timestamp":1794740052598},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed proofs work correctly - they don't trigger the pending check even if the attestation is old.\n\nNow let me also test the edge case where the OTS file is missing (which should still be caught as before):","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Confirmed proofs work correctly - they don't trigger the pending check even if the attestation is old.\\n\\nNow let me also test the edge case where the OTS file is missing (which should still be caught as before):\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed proofs work correctly. Let me also verify the existing \"missing OTS proof\" check still works:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-78e926a3-1c06-4419-81c8-551642af64cd","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport tempfile, os, json, hashlib, time, io, contextlib, sys\nimport record as R\n\n# Create a test ledger\nd = tempfile.mkdtemp()\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'entries'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'anchors'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'inbox'))\n\n# Create two entries\nchain = []\nfor i in range(2):\n    kind = 'plan'\n    body = {'by': 'test', 'claim': f'claim {i+1}', 'test': 'test', 'decision_rule': 'rule'}\n    e = R.make_entry(chain, kind, body, now='2024-01-01T00:00:00Z')\n    raw = R.canonical(e)\n    with open(os.path.join(d, 'entries', f'{e[\\\"seq\\\"]:06d}.json'), 'wb') as f:\n        f.write(raw)\n    chain.append((e, hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()))\n\n# Create a sigstore anchor for entry 2 (range head) but NO ots file\nold_time = int(time.time()) - 73 * 3600  # 73 hours ago\n\n# Create dummy sigstore file\nwith open(os.path.join(d, 'anchors', '000002.sigstore.json'), 'w') as f:\n    f.write('{}')\n\n# Stub the functions\noriginal_check_sigstore = R.check_sigstore\noriginal_check_ots = R.check_ots\n\ndef stub_check_sigstore(*args, **kwargs):\n    pred = R.range_predicate(chain, 1, 2)\n    return (old_time, pred, 'abc123')\n\ndef stub_check_ots(*args, **kwargs):\n    return None  # pending (won't be called since no ots file)\n\nR.check_sigstore = stub_check_sigstore\nR.check_ots = stub_check_ots\n\ndef run_cmd(*args):\n    out, err = io.StringIO(), io.StringIO()\n    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(out), contextlib.redirect_stderr(err):\n        rc = R.main(['--ledger', d, *args])\n    return rc, out.getvalue(), err.getvalue()\n\ntry:\n    # Test with --max-pending-hours 72 but missing ots file (should fail with missing proof error)\n    rc, out, err = run_cmd('check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '72')\n    print(f'Missing OTS with --max-pending-hours 72: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\nfinally:\n    R.check_sigstore = original_check_sigstore\n    R.check_ots = original_check_ots\n    import shutil\n    shutil.rmtree(d)\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":3944,"output":729,"cacheRead":26304,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":45,"totalTokens":30977,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794740052599,"responseId":"gen-1794740052-pXUqESIP0AgSpkWOGGkf","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":11679,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-78e926a3-1c06-4419-81c8-551642af64cd","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Missing OTS with --max-pending-hours 72: rc=1\n  stderr: BAD: anchors/000002.ots is missing, though the writer stamps every range head before attesting\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":57,"timestamp":1794740064337},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The missing OTS proof check still works correctly.\n\nNow let me run the full test suite again to make sure everything still passes.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The missing OTS proof check still works correctly.\\n\\nNow let me run the full test suite again to make sure everything still passes.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The missing OTS proof check still works. Let me run the full test suite one more time to confirm everything passes:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-05017b00-8f2f-4c66-b9b5-94764c13d6ef","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -m unittest test_record -v"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":353,"output":88,"cacheRead":30688,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":26,"totalTokens":311